["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"bin Laden Was Not Born Extreme: Three Turns Pushed Him Onto the Jihadist Road bin Laden was not an extremist as a child but a marginal figure in a wealthy Saudi family; three turning points — the 1979 Mecca siege, the Afghan battlefield and the Gulf War — put him on the road to global jihad, and he always wanted to bring down the Saudi royal family more than he wanted to fight the United States alone. Dan Snow&#x27;s History Hit History Hit The Making of Osama bin Laden History of terrorism al-Qaeda bin Laden Middle East politics War on Terror Wahhabi Mujahideen Muslim Brotherhood Tora Bora\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-historyhit-本-拉登的极端化是选择不是宿命/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f67d4b795a40fffd3b2c/1786636082162-9c939840-0417-4daa-8462-7e282931a6db.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"D\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Dan Snow&#x27;s History Hit</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>bin Laden Was Not Born Extreme: Three Turns Pushed Him Onto the Jihadist Road</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">bin Laden was not an extremist as a child but a marginal figure in a wealthy Saudi family; three turning points — the 1979 Mecca siege, the Afghan battlefield and the Gulf War — put him on the road to global jihad, and he always wanted to bring down the Saudi royal family more than he wanted to fight the United States alone.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">History of terrorism</span><span class=\"tag\">al-Qaeda</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"China&#x27;s EV industry wasn&#x27;t planned into existence — local credit bought the right of way This episode takes half the credit for the rise of China&#x27;s carmakers away from central industrial policy: the real engine was local governments trading loans and equity for factories, and entrepreneurs using relationships to route around SOE licensing — at the cost of an overcapacity nobody can now unwind. ChinaTalk ChinaTalk The Rise of China’s Electric Vehicle Industry EVs Local government Industrial policy Overcapacity Exports SOE reform three bigs and three smalls township and village enterprise (TVE) 10 city thousand vehicle project Hefei model special purpose vehicle (SPV)\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-chinatalk-中国电动车不是北京规划出来的-是地方政府用信贷买路权买出来的/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/d33ffece-99d8-11f1-8cc6-f328fc037173/image/b16c651d8b1a202e90a15ea6dc470b88.jpeg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:54:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\">ChinaTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>China&#x27;s EV industry wasn&#x27;t planned into existence — local credit bought the right of way</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">This episode takes half the credit for the rise of China&#x27;s carmakers away from central industrial policy: the real engine was local governments trading loans and equity for factories, and entrepreneurs using relationships to route around SOE licensing — at the cost of an overcapacity nobody can now unwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">EVs</span><span class=\"tag\">Local government</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"When a child asks permission for everything, the problem is perfectionism, not the child A four-and-a-half-year-old boy comes home from preschool and starts asking permission for everything; his mother finds that when she sets perfectionism aside and stops handing him answers, his ability to solve problems on his own far exceeds what she expected. Your Parenting Mojo Your Parenting Mojo Re-release: Creative Problem-Solving (Without Giving the Answer) Interest-led learning Perfectionism Scaffolding questions Metacognition Nature school lantern consciousness yes space learning exploration scaffolding metacognition\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-17-parentmojo-孩子不需要你给出答案-只需要一个脚手架/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://artwork.captivate.fm/12802a36-dbca-4912-a62e-cbce5aacddb8/podcast-cover-your-parenting-mojo-03-01-copy.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">54:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Your Parenting Mojo</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0817</span></div>\n<h2>When a child asks permission for everything, the problem is perfectionism, not the child</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A four-and-a-half-year-old boy comes home from preschool and starts asking permission for everything; his mother finds that when she sets perfectionism aside and stops handing him answers, his ability to solve problems on his own far exceeds what she expected.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Interest-led learning</span><span class=\"tag\">Perfectionism</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"The Troubles were not a religious war but demographic anxiety and zero-sum politics For decades Britain ignored the demographic anxiety and economic imbalance inside Northern Ireland and left the problem to the streets; in the summer of 1966, while Londoners cared only about the World Cup, the violence in Ulster was about to run out of control. The Rest Is History The Rest Is History 697. The Troubles: Murder in Belfast (Part 1) The Troubles British politics Nationalism Sectarian conflict The 1960s Paisley The Troubles\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-restishistory-北爱冲突不是宗教战争-而是人口与经济的零和博弈/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/00c0a118-2426-11ee-b258-73d331d0123b/image/db3295fcd9d3a7113e8000e931f0541d.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:26:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Rest Is History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>The Troubles were not a religious war but demographic anxiety and zero-sum politics</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">For decades Britain ignored the demographic anxiety and economic imbalance inside Northern Ireland and left the problem to the streets; in the summer of 1966, while Londoners cared only about the World Cup, the violence in Ulster was about to run out of control.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">The Troubles</span><span class=\"tag\">British politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"TSMC Trucks Half-Finished Wafers Between Fabs: The Secret Weapon of AI Capacity TSMC exploits the more than 90% tool overlap between N5 and N7 to truck half-processed wafers from its Tainan fab to Taichung for finishing, freeing up AI capacity while N5 converts to N3. The foundation of the AI boom is a fleet of ordinary trucks. Asianometry Asianometry How TSMC Uses Old Fabs to Make New Chips TSMC Chip capacity Advanced packaging AI compute Semiconductor manufacturing Cross-node utilization cross-node utilization gate-all-around (GAA) back end of the line (BEOL) CoWoS FOUP\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-asianometry-台积电用货车把旧厂改造成-ai-新产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/cDxVYQrxeiQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">15:47</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0816</span></div>\n<h2>TSMC Trucks Half-Finished Wafers Between Fabs: The Secret Weapon of AI Capacity</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">TSMC exploits the more than 90% tool overlap between N5 and N7 to truck half-processed wafers from its Tainan fab to Taichung for finishing, freeing up AI capacity while N5 converts to N3. The foundation of the AI boom is a fleet of ordinary trucks.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">TSMC</span><span class=\"tag\">Chip capacity</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Anti-vaccine sentiment is not new: Jenner&#x27;s own book is full of people cursing him This episode shows the anti-vaccine movement is as old as vaccines themselves; phage SPO1 uses liquid-liquid phase-separated condensates to switch transcriptional phases; ancient smallpox DNA from South America confirms transmission by European colonization; and declining reading plus AI-generated content threaten our powers of discernment. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1349: Smallpox and mummies Phage Vaccines Smallpox Phase separation Anti-vaccine Transcriptional regulation liquid-liquid phase separation (LLPS) intrinsically disordered region (IDR) biomolecular condensate RNA polymerase holoenzyme vaccinia virus factory synonymous substitution rate\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-16-twiv-反疫苗古已有之-噬菌体凝聚体是转录调控核心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">2:03:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker