its mines ran almost entirely on enslaved people; after Carthage fell in 146 BC slavery became the engine of the economy, and once Augustus stopped expanding, that population reproduced itself by birth.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Roman history</span><span class=\"tag\">Slavery</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"America Rescued the Yen for Its Own Trillion in Treasuries, Not for Japan The first US intervention in the yen in 28 years was officially a favor to an ally. The real calculation was to stop Japan from selling $1 trillion of US Treasuries to defend its currency — which would push up America&#x27;s own cost of borrowing. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle The Hidden Risk in the US-Japan Yen Rescue US Treasuries Japanese yen FX intervention US Treasury Interest rates Carry trade carry trade forward premium puzzle Cakeism Treasury Convenience Yield\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-15-patrickboyle-美国救日元不是为日本-是为自家万亿美债/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://d3t3ozftmdmh3i.cloudfront.net/staging/podcast_uploaded_nologo/42184536/48d3d010465c2cda.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">31:36</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0815</span></div>\n<h2>America Rescued the Yen for Its Own Trillion in Treasuries, Not for Japan</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The first US intervention in the yen in 28 years was officially a favor to an ally. The real calculation was to stop Japan from selling $1 trillion of US Treasuries to defend its currency — which would push up America&#x27;s own cost of borrowing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">US Treasuries</span><span class=\"tag\">Japanese yen</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"The Order Calls Vaccines Soda and Splits MMR Into More Shots: Every Sentence Is a Lie Every sentence in the ‘gold standard’ executive order gets called a lie: splitting MMR to add needles, vaccines as bottled soda, Merck refusing outright — and the new CDC director will have to pick a side. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1348: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Vaccine policy MMR Outbreak data Parasites Long COVID Wastewater surveillance MMR / measles-mumps-rubella vaccine ACIP / Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices lyophilized PICO / the PICO question framework sterile insect technique RIG / rabies immune globulin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-15-twiv-行政令里的谎言-拆mmr与汽水比喻都是伪科学/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">55:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0815</span></div>\n<h2>The Order Calls Vaccines Soda and Splits MMR Into More Shots: Every Sentence Is a Lie</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Every sentence in the ‘gold standard’ executive order gets called a lie: splitting MMR to add needles, vaccines as bottled soda, Merck refusing outright — and the new CDC director will have to pick a side.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Vaccine policy</span><span class=\"tag\">MMR</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"parent\"\n data-hay=\"The cure for picky-eating anxiety: no judgment, no rewards, dessert is just another food A child&#x27;s relationship with food does not hinge on whether they ate any particular thing. It hinges on whether the parent sorts food into good and bad, whether dessert gets used as a reward, and whether the parent gives themselves permission to feed according to what the child actually needs. The earlier picky-eating signals are recognized, the easier they are to change. Raising Good Humans Raising Good Humans Picky Eating &amp; Food Guilt with Jennifer Anderson Child feeding Picky eating Food anxiety Parent-child communication Body image Feeding psychology embodied independence hyper-palatable foods PSAE\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-raisinggh-挑食焦虑的解药-不评判-不奖励-甜点也是普通食物/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/216d7bb0-95d0-11f1-b9ad-6f2d14c4eade/image/6786871cff0ea61c3f706ebdda40515e.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"R\"><span class=\"dur\">46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"parent\"><span class=\"src\">Raising Good Humans</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>The cure for picky-eating anxiety: no judgment, no rewards, dessert is just another food</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A child&#x27;s relationship with food does not hinge on whether they ate any particular thing. It hinges on whether the parent sorts food into good and bad, whether dessert gets used as a reward, and whether the parent gives themselves permission to feed according to what the child actually needs. The earlier picky-eating signals are recognized, the easier they are to change.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Child feeding</span><span class=\"tag\">Picky eating</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\"\n data-hay=\"Straight women&#x27;s dating pessimism isn&#x27;t melodrama — it&#x27;s political rollback and economic dependence Sarah Jones argues that straight women&#x27;s awkwardness and pessimism about dating men is both genuine feeling and performance, sitting on top of political rollback, economic dependence, and a reality that social media amplifies. The Gray Area with Sean Illing The Gray Area Why straight dating feels bleak Heteropessimism Gender politics Dating culture Women&#x27;s bind Social commentary heteropessimism hopeful pessimism\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-grayarea-异性恋悲观主义-直女困境的真实与表演/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/a2ed43cc-fe19-11f0-8400-b7049bc68c1c/image/09d3576515488959f432d219d5c7416b.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">57:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Gray Area with Sean Illing</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Straight women&#x27;s dating pessimism isn&#x27;t melodrama — it&#x27;s political rollback and economic dependence</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Sarah Jones argues that straight women&#x27;s awkwardness and pessimism about dating men is both genuine feeling and performance, sitting on top of political rollback, economic dependence, and a reality that social media amplifies.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>2</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Heteropessimism</span><span class=\"tag\">Gender politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\"\n data-hay=\"El Niño Isn&#x27;t a Short-Term Shock, It&#x27;s a Permanent Loss of Growth El Niño is not just a passing weather shock: research shows it permanently depresses the path of economic growth, a single strong event can cost trillions of dollars within five years, and we have not adapted to it. Odd Lots Odd Lots A Historic El Niño Is Coming That Could Cost the World Trillions El Niño Climate economics Economic growth Global warming Adaptation strategy ENSO / El Niño-Southern Oscillation Teleconnection RONI / Relative Oceanic Niño Index Level effect\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-oddlots-厄尔尼诺不是短期冲击-而是永久性增长损失/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.omnycontent.com/d/playlist/e73c998e-6e60-432f-8610-ae210140c5b1/8a94442e-5a74-4fa2-8b8d-ae27003a8d6b/982f5071-765c-403d-969d-ae27003a8d83/image.jpg?t=1681322812&amp;size=Medium\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">55:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>El Niño Isn&#x27;t a Short-Term Shock, It&#x27;s a Permanent Loss of Growth</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">El Niño is not just a passing weather shock: research shows it permanently depresses the path of economic growth, a single strong event can cost trillions of dollars within five years, and we have not adapted to it.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">El Niño</span><span class=\"tag\">Climate economics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"Lindy Runs Entirely on DeepSeek; Its Founder Wants Chinese Models Banned Flo Crivello says the driver of Lindy&#x27;s whole agent stack is now DeepSeek — while he simultaneously argues the entire industry should be banned from using it, because competitors will use it and so he has to, and he&#x27;d rather see that prisoner&#x27;s dilemma solved by coordination. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution Lindy Teammate: Flo Crivello on Multiplayer Agents, Memory &amp; Why He&#x27;d Ban the Chinese Models He Uses Agent memory Context engineering Inference cost Chinese models Enterprise sales Prompt optimization hydration context bucket centary tree TOON hypothesis driven retrieval per-user LoRA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-14-cogrev-lindy-全线跑在-deepseek-上-创始人主张封禁中国模型/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/67f4c75e-93d8-11f1-bc73-4b7840ced6dd/image/4b0b55cbbf397c80de476a6b6e5e6d36.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:06:53</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0814</span></div>\n<h2>Lindy Runs Entirely on DeepSeek; Its Founder Wants Chinese Models Banned</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Flo Crivello says the driver of Lindy&#x27;s whole agent stack is now DeepSeek — while he simultaneously argues the entire industry should be banned from using it, because competitors will use it and so he has to, and he&#x27;d rather see that prisoner&#x27;s dilemma solved by coordination.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>12</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Agent memory</span><span class=\"tag\">Context engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\"\n data-hay=\"SK hynix&#x27;s turnaround ran on customer relationships, not on HBM technology SK hynix&#x27;s comeback was not a bet on HBM as a technology but a bet on customer relationships and sustained investment; Samsung, betting on PIM for edge inference, happened to hand its rival the sole-supplier position at the ChatGPT moment. Asianometry Asianometry SK hynix and the HBM Revolution Semiconductors HBM Memory chips Korean chaebol Advanced packaging AI compute HBM / High Bandwidth Memory TSV / Through Silicon Via TC-NCF / Thermal Compression with Non-Conductive Film MR-MUF / Mass Reflow Molded Underfill HBM-PIM / Processing-in-Memory ADR / American Depositary Receipt\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-asianometry-sk-hynix-靠-hbm-翻身-客户战略赢过周期/\">\