ate\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>A single robot model matches fine-tuned specialists out of the box</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">One robot model now matches task-tuned specialists zero-shot, and above all composes learned skills onto robot arms it has never seen — all of it resting on using prompts to tame low-quality, heterogeneous data. The bottleneck is shifting to reliability, speed and physical distribution.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Embodied AI</span><span class=\"tag\">Robot models</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\"\n data-hay=\"Did a Substation Wreck the 49ers? The Dose Is 40x Too Low, and the Data Says No The conspiracy theory that electromagnetic radiation from a substation caused the 49ers&#x27; injury wave gets dismantled point by point by radiation experts and injury databases: the dose is far below the safety threshold, the cited papers don&#x27;t hold up, the 2014 expansion was a different substation, and the data doesn&#x27;t show the 49ers are the worst off. Science Vs Science Vs We Solve the 49ers Viral Conspiracy Theory NFL Injury data EMF radiation Conspiracy theories Fact-checking Oxidative stress milligauss deep story\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-sciencevs-变电站不背这口锅-49人队伤病阴谋论被拆穿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/f521b120-2c30-11e6-b5f3-63ee984ee1a4/image/e7470287efbfa0aff068175bb6c31805.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:01:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Science Vs</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Did a Substation Wreck the 49ers? The Dose Is 40x Too Low, and the Data Says No</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The 