lently; who the bank makes absorb the loss matters more than teaching users to spot phishing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">LLMs</span><span class=\"tag\">Anti-fraud</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Romans knew the founding myth was false and used it as a diplomatic tool Rome&#x27;s origin myths were not history carved in stone but an elastic narrative Romans used to negotiate, to absorb other peoples, and to digest civil war; the archaeology even contradicts the 753 BC founding date outright. The Ancients The Ancients Romulus &amp; Remus Roman history Political mythology Archaeology Aeneas Romulus Oral tradition Rex Pomerium Casa Romuli Lupa\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-13-ancients-罗马人清楚建城神话是虚构的-但照样当外交工具/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://assets.pippa.io/shows/6215f9e74b795a6299fd3b58/1786360459782-d4158422-9610-4d6e-9464-82ce00eea17a.jpeg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">59:55</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0813</span></div>\n<h2>Romans knew the founding myth was false and used it as a diplomatic tool</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Rome&#x27;s origin myths were not history carved in stone but an elastic narrative Romans used to negotiate, to absorb other peoples, and to digest civil war; the archaeology even contradicts the 753 BC founding date outright.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Roman history</span><span class=\"tag\">Political mythology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\"\n data-hay=\"Elizabeth wanted Mary assassinated, but was forced to sign the death warrant Elizabeth I did not want Mary executed in public; she hoped someone would kill her privately under the Bond of Association. The Privy Council insisted on legal process, and in the end, even after the Queen had signed, they defied her wishes and rushed the warrant through the night to Fotheringhay. The Rest Is History The Rest Is History 696. Elizabeth I vs The Catholics: Killing the Queen of Scots (Part 6) Elizabeth I Mary Stuart British history Intelligence war Cryptography Death penalty politics Bond of Association Act for the Queen&#x27;s Safety presence chamber Star Chamber cipher\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-12-restishistory-玛丽之死背后的真博弈-伊丽莎白想要暗杀-不想签字/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://megaphone.imgix.net/podcasts/00c0a118-2426-11ee-b258-73d331d0123b/image/db3295fcd9d3a7113e8000e931f0541d.jpg?ixlib=rails-4.3.1&amp;max-w=3000&amp;max-h=3000&amp;fit=crop&amp;auto=format,compress&amp;w=400&amp;auto=format\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:09:49</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Rest Is History</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0812</span></div>\n<h2>Elizabeth wanted Mary assassinated, but was forced to sign the death warrant</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Elizabeth I did not want Mary executed in public; she hoped someone would kill her privately under the Bond of Association. The Privy Council insisted on legal process, and in the end, even after the Queen had signed, they defied her wishes and rushed the warrant through the night to Fotheringhay.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Elizabeth I</span><span class=\"tag\">Mary Stuart</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\"\n data-hay=\"NVIDIA&#x27;s VP of Research: The Endgame for Models Is Ecosystem, Not Beating Rivals Ming-Yu Liu: model capabilities will eventually converge